324-## 6. API surface & SSE event shape (frozen)
325-
326-Routes exactly as the spec lists (`/api/workflows` CRUD+import/export; `/api/workflow/node-types|validate|run|executions/*`). New blueprint `workflows_bp`, name `"workflows"`, **no url_prefix** (matches all 14 existing blueprints), imported and registered with the other blueprints in `app.py`. Provider-backed option resolution occurs at request time after startup initialization; blueprint registration itself must not assume populated provider registries.
327-
328-All endpoints are local-app endpoints and enforce `is_loopback_remote`; mutation endpoints also
329-require JSON content types where applicable. Success payloads are JSON objects rather than bare
330-arrays. Errors use one envelope everywhere:
331-
332-```json
333-{
334-  "error": {
335-    "code": "WORKFLOW_INVALID",
336-    "message": "Workflow has validation errors",
337-    "details": { "problems": [] }
338-  }
339-}
340-```
341-
342-`details` is optional and redacted. Expected endpoint contracts:
343-
344-| endpoint | request | success |
345-|---|---|---|
346-| `GET /api/workflows` | optional `limit` 1–200 (default 100) | `200 {workflows:[summary], total:n}` sorted by `updated_at` descending then ID; no pagination until the 200-item cap is insufficient |
347-| `POST /api/workflows` | `{workflow:<definition without server id/timestamps>}` | `201 {workflow}` + `Location`; server allocates ID/timestamps |
348-| `GET /api/workflows/<id>` | — | `200 {workflow}`; `404` if absent |
349-| `PUT /api/workflows/<id>` | `{workflow, expected_updated_at}` | `200 {workflow}`; `409 WORKFLOW_CONFLICT` on stale update |
350:| `DELETE /api/workflows/<id>` | `{expected_updated_at?}` | `200 {deleted:true, workflow_id}` after atomic move to trash; `409` on stale update |
351-| `POST /api/workflows/import` | `{workflow, on_conflict:"reject"|"new_id"}` | `201 {workflow, imported_from_id?}`; default `new_id` |
352-| `GET /api/workflows/<id>/export` | — | `200 application/json` definition with attachment filename; no execution data/secrets |
353-| `GET /api/workflow/node-types` | — | `200 {registry_version, node_types, port_types}` with no executor/callable internals |
354-| `GET /api/workflow/templates` | — | `200 {templates:[{template_id, workflow}]}`; every bundled graph passes server validation |
355-| `POST /api/workflow/validate` | `{workflow}` | `200 {valid, problems, warnings}` for a well-formed request, even when graph-invalid; malformed transport is `400` |
356-| `POST /api/workflow/run` | `{workflow_id xor workflow, run_mode, target_node_ids:[], force:false, project_id?}` | `202 {execution_id, project_id, status:"queued"}` |
357-| `POST /api/workflow/executions/<id>/stop` | `{}` | `202 {execution_id, status:"cancelling"}`; `409` if already terminal |
358-| `GET /api/workflow/executions/<id>` | — | `200 {execution}`; `404` if absent |
359-| `GET /api/workflow/executions/<id>/events` | standard `Last-Event-ID` on reconnect | `200 text/event-stream`; `404` if absent |
360-| `GET /api/workflow/executions` | required `workflow_id`, optional `limit` 1–200 | `200 {executions:[summary], total:n}` sorted newest first |
361-| `GET /api/workflows/<id>/webhook` | — | `200 {webhook, token, path}` with `Cache-Control: no-store`; creates the separately persisted token when absent |
362-| `POST /api/workflows/<id>/webhook/regenerate` | `{}` | `200 {token, path}` with `Cache-Control: no-store`; immediately invalidates the prior URL |
363-| `POST /api/workflow/hooks/<id>/<token>` | mapped JSON object, max 64 KiB | `202 {execution_id, project_id, status:"queued"}` with queue source `webhook`; available only to loopback clients while the server itself is loopback-bound |
364-
365-Create/import/save return `422 WORKFLOW_INVALID` when the JSON transport is valid but violates
366-workflow rules. Use `400` for malformed JSON/request shape, `403` for non-loopback access,
367-`404` for missing resources, `409` for conflicts/locks/terminal stop, `413` for size limits,
368-and `500` only for unexpected redacted server failures. Add `WORKFLOW_CONFLICT` to the stable
369-error-code set.
370-
371-SSE (own emitter in `studio/workflows/events.py` — do NOT reuse pipeline `_emit`, which is private and closes over `_jobs`; see blocker B6):
372-
373-```jsonc
374-{ "sequence": 12, "execution_id": "ex_123", "node_id": "n_tts",
375-  "status": "running", "attempt": 1, "timestamp": "ISO",
376-  "duration_ms": 0, "summary": "Generating narration",
377-  "progress": {"ready": 3, "total": 10},      // optional, poll-driven nodes
378-  "from_sample_data": false }                  // present when stub-fed
379-```
380-Monotonic `sequence` per execution; each SSE frame includes `id: <sequence>` and a JSON `data:` payload. The stream ends on terminal event `{node_id: null, status: "succeeded|failed|cancelled"}`. On automatic reconnect, browser `EventSource` sends the standard `Last-Event-ID` header; the server replays events with greater sequence values from a bounded ring (1000 events). If the requested ID predates the retained buffer, emit a snapshot/reset event before live events. The client also deduplicates by `sequence`.
